assert failed: the untaken overflowing arm does not poison the selected value
Blocker: chelis#1464. That issue's own reproducer is a TAKEN `fail` arm
replaced by zero; this probe is the sibling symptom -- an UNTAKEN arithmetic
arm that overflows and poisons the select. Same root cause and the same
spec/06 §2.10.1 rule ("untaken branches are not evaluated"). #1464's
acceptance already covers this case ("untaken branch: forward value and
gradient remain unchanged across lanes"); this probe is the reproducer that
bullet did not have.
On pass, drop the series-input clamp in `Nautilus.Special.erf` (and the
symmetry clamp in `erf_t`), re-run tests/special.ch's
test_erf_series_arm_survives_a_vmapped_huge_input, and archive the
chelis#1464 entry in docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md in the same change set.
